- `blanket-suppression` (python, rust): Flags suppression directives that name no rule.
- `dynamic-attribute-access` (python): Flags `getattr`, `hasattr`, `setattr` and `delattr` calls in Python.
- `edit-of-described-commit` (command): Blocks `jj edit` on a commit that already has a description.
- `environment-variable-in-function` (python, rust): Flags environment variable access inside functions.
- `error-log-in-except` (python): Flags `logging.error` calls inside Python `except` blocks.
- `identical-positional-types` (python): Flags Python functions whose positional parameters share a type annotation.
- `missing-suppression-reason` (python, rust): Requires every suppression directive to give a reason.
- `mock-call-assertion` (python): Flags assertions on how a mock was called in Python tests.
- `mock-in-tests` (python): Flags dynamic mocks and monkeypatching in Python tests.
- `mutable-dataclass` (python): Requires Python dataclasses to declare `frozen=True`.
- `nested-function` (python): Flags Python functions defined inside other functions.
- `packed-assertion` (python, rust): Flags assertions that pack several checks into one condition.
- `primitive-duration` (python, rust): Flags variable names that carry a time unit, such as `timeout_secs` or `delay_ms`.
- `repeated-index-access` (python, rust): Flags a value read at several literal positions instead of being unpacked once.
- `single-letter-name` (python, rust): Flags names made of a single letter.
- `sleep-in-tests` (python, rust): Flags fixed-duration sleeps in tests.
- `suppressed-exception` (python): Requires a comment explaining each `contextlib.suppress` block.
- `too-many-assertions` (python, rust): Limits the number of assertions in one test function.
- `type-cast` (python): Flags `typing.cast` calls in Python production code.
- `type-suffixed-name` (python, rust): Flags variable names that end with a type suffix such as `_list` or `_str`.
- `unknown-suppression-rule` (python, rust): Flags suppression directives that name an unknown or unsuppressible rule.
- `unslotted-dataclass` (python): Requires Python dataclasses to declare `slots=True`.
- `unstructured-task` (python): Flags asyncio tasks spawned outside a task group.
- `unused-suppression` (python, rust): Flags suppression directives that suppress no finding.
- `zero-sleep-in-tests` (python, rust): Flags zero-duration sleeps used to yield in tests.

